    <fr:title text="The anomaly law">The anomaly law</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
    <fr:meta name="area">symplectic</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="avatar">3</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="status">open</fr:meta>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>(anomaly law). Coisotropy of the survivor cocycle fails only at special
characteristic-2 germs.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Role in the skeleton.</html:strong> The law is the bookkeeping for why characteristic 2 is the sole
obstruction to characteristic-free statements at germ scale — which
germs are anomalous, and why only generic statements survive there.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Open. Measured on the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D_4]]></fr:tex> moment-map probes. Consistent with
the small-<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> record: the one genuine counterexample to a
naively-stated survivor identity in the whole program is over <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathbb {F}_q]]></fr:tex>
with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q = 2]]></fr:tex> at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 5]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0017/" title="Wall 1: coisotropy of the cyclic cocycle" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0017/" display-uri="ffi-0017" type="local">Wall 1: coisotropy of the cyclic cocycle</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0049/" title="The germ apparatus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0049/" display-uri="ffi-0049" type="local">The germ apparatus</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p>
      <html:em>Provenance: journal passes 6--8 (variational identities, thresholds,
anomaly law); distilled.tex Part 5.</html:em>
    </html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
