            <fr:title text="Wall 1: coisotropy of the cyclic cocycle">Wall 1: coisotropy of the cyclic cocycle</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">symplectic</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="avatar">3</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Wall 1. The cyclic cocycle carried by the survivor algebra of a
pencil germ is coisotropic.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Role in the skeleton.</html:strong> This is the bottom floor of the avatar tower: the germ-scale
instance of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0013/" title="The thesis: every bound is half an orbit dimension" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0013/" display-uri="ffi-0013" type="local">the thesis</fr:link>, and the fixed point from which
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0050/" title="(W): the wall conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0050/" display-uri="ffi-0050" type="local">(W)</fr:link> tries to upgrade coisotropy to the full Lagrangian
statement. It is a theorem; the upgrade is not.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0011/" title="The trace form" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0011/" display-uri="ffi-0011" type="local">The trace form</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0049/" title="The germ apparatus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0049/" display-uri="ffi-0049" type="local">The germ apparatus</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal pass 6--8 apparatus (Borel/Steinberg, Wall 1);
distilled.tex Part 5.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
